  "designNotes": "The ore source outruns one smelter but the plates must also merge back into one belt, and there is no room for the usual fork-and-rejoin. Place the splitter so the smelters plug straight into its outputs, then choose which side the plates come out on so the merger meets the belt to the demand. The rock beside the source rules out a west smelter; dropping the splitter onto the top row instead trims the footprint (36 vs 42) for one extra belt.",
